  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Designed, illustrated, and printed by Russell Maret.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The primary volume is in an accordion-style format, with the first half of the book printed on one side, and the second half on the other. The book must be turned to read through. The secondary volume, State proofs, is printed on double leaves and specifcally for copy XI. Issued together in a clamshell box.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"There are three editions: Seventy-five copies, numbered 1-71 and AP1-AP4, are printed on mould-made Zerkall Litho 270gm paper ... Sixteen copies, numbered I-XIII and API-APIII, are printed on specially devised cotton and abaca Twinrocker handmade paper, made by Travis Becker. They are bound in full leather with seven color leather inlays, and accompanied by a second volume of state and progressive proofs of the proposition matching the book's number .... One copy, lettered E ... is accompanied by a complete, unbound set of state &amp; progressive proofs ..."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
